Forum for WoltLab Suite
=======================

A discussion forum (boards, threads, posts) for WoltLab Suite Core 6.2.
It is an independent implementation, installed as the application
package "com.tinsever.forum".

Status: beta (1.0.0 Beta 1). Expect bugs and do not run it on a
production site without a backup.

This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by WoltLab GmbH.
"WoltLab" and "WoltLab Suite" are trademarks of WoltLab GmbH.


Features
--------

  * Board list with categories, nested categories, collapsible
    sections, statistics, users online and moderators
  * Board pages with sortable thread lists and announcements
  * Thread pages with quick reply, inline editing, quotes, mentions,
    attachments, polls, reactions, tags and share links
  * Moderation: move, split, copy, merge, close, disable and trash
    threads and posts, including bulk actions; thread log and ACP
    modification log
  * Per-board permissions (ACL) next to the global group permissions
  * Unread, latest, unanswered, undone, watched and participated
    thread lists; thread subscriptions and notifications
  * Boxes: thread list, hot threads, board list, forum statistics
  * Search, sitemaps, RSS feeds of threads and RSS feed import
  * Article discussions in forum threads
  * Account switcher for linked user accounts
  * Data importers compatible with exporters written for
    WoltLab Burning Board (com.woltlab.wbb.*)
  * English and German translations


Requirements
------------

  * WoltLab Suite Core 6.2.x (6.3 is not supported yet)
  * PHP and database as required by WoltLab Suite Core 6.2
    (PHP 8.1.2 to 8.4.x)


Installation
------------

1. Download com.tinsever.forum.tar from
   https://codeberg.org/tinsever/woltlab-forum/releases
   or build it yourself (see "Building" below).
2. In the ACP, go to Configuration > Packages > Install Package and
   upload the archive.
3. Create your boards under Forum > Boards.

Updating works the same way: upload the newer archive and WoltLab
Suite runs the update. All 1.0.0 Alpha and Beta versions can update to
the latest release.


Building
--------

    ./scripts/build-package.sh

This writes build/packages/com.tinsever.forum.tar.

Codeberg CI (.forgejo/workflows/ci.yml) lints the code on PHP 8.1 and
8.4, checks the generated files and builds the package on every push;
the archive is attached to each run as an artifact.

To publish a release, bump <version> in forum/package.xml and push a
matching tag: "1.0.0 Beta 2" becomes v1.0.0-beta.2, "1.0.0" becomes
v1.0.0. CI then creates the release with the package attached. If the
built-in token cannot create releases, add a repository secret
RELEASE_TOKEN with write:repository scope.


Development
-----------

The scripts set up a local WoltLab Suite install in developer mode,
served by PHP's built-in web server. You need PHP 8.2 (or any version
WSC 6.2 supports), MariaDB/MySQL, git, rsync and Python 3.

1. Fetch the WoltLab sources into vendor-ref/:

       ./scripts/fetch-vendor.sh

2. Create a database user that may create the database "wsc".
   The defaults are user "wsc" / password "wsc" on 127.0.0.1; override
   them with DB_HOST, DB_USER and DB_PASSWORD.

3. Install everything from scratch (this DROPS the "wsc" database):

       ./scripts/dev-reinstall.sh

   The server listens on port 80 because the WSC frontend does not
   accept a non-default port. Set PHP_BIN if php is not at
   /opt/homebrew/opt/php@8.2/bin/php. The router only accepts requests
   from localhost.

   Frontend: http://localhost/wsc/forum/
   ACP:      http://localhost/wsc/acp/
   Logins:   dev / root (admin), alice / alice, bob / bob

Day-to-day scripts:

  scripts/dev-server.sh start|stop   start or stop the web server
  scripts/dev-sync.sh                copy PHP, JS, CSS and templates into
                                     the dev install
  scripts/dev_sync_pips.py [url] [pip ...]
                                     re-apply XML and language PIPs
                                     without losing data
  scripts/dev_worker.py CLASS ...    run rebuild-data workers
  scripts/install_package.py TAR     install a package archive via the ACP
  scripts/uninstall_package.py ID    uninstall a package
  scripts/check-phrases.sh           list phrases that are used but missing
  scripts/lint.sh                    PHP syntax and XML well-formedness

Language files and permission XML are generated. Edit the tables in
scripts/gen/ and run:

    python3 scripts/gen/language.py
    python3 scripts/gen/permissions.py

When releasing a version that removes files, templates or pages, list
them in fileDelete.xml, templateDelete.xml or the <delete> block of
page.xml, and bump <version> in package.xml.


Layout
------

  forum/            package source (package.xml, PIP XML files)
    files/          application files (PHP, JS, SCSS)
    files_wcf/      files installed into the WCF directory
    templates/      frontend templates
    acptemplates/   ACP templates
    language/       en.xml, de.xml (generated)
  scripts/          build and development helpers
  vendor-ref/       WoltLab sources (not tracked, see fetch-vendor.sh)
  build/, dev/      build output and local install (not tracked)


